The two base configurations in this directory are Debian's own, byte for byte, unpacked from the Debian package
linux-config-7.2 7.2.9-1 (the amd64 file of that source package):

  debian-7.2.9-amd64.config      = usr/src/linux-config-7.2/config.amd64_none_amd64.xz      (baseline and v3 flavours)
      sha256 247d3e6a63e853d87496c1752d6ecb7278e3839bcc3b2277bb7532621864e91f
  debian-7.2.9-rt-amd64.config   = usr/src/linux-config-7.2/config.amd64_none_rt-amd64.xz   (rt flavour)
      sha256 1547e1d78ea86c60f62340928f9fb172ee926598f96df00ad00656932ad4aec7

  package   pool/main/l/linux/linux-config-7.2_7.2.9-1_amd64.deb   (Debian unstable on 2026-10-08; testing had 7.2.8-1)
  sha256    04fdd2602df31676fcd63b34727ee6274c2a2cdc8f076b2676706f9cc2e463a7
  source    Debian kernel team, https://salsa.debian.org/kernel-team/linux (tag debian/7.2.9-1), GPL-2.0

To move to a newer Debian configuration: unpack the new linux-config-7.x package, replace the two files, run
kernel/tests/config-proof.sh for every flavour, and read the table it prints (options that stopped holding, options gone
from the tree, new defaults).
